outputs/

# The local knowledge-graph working directory. Every `crib index` rewrites thousands of files here,
# which buried real code changes under ~4,700 generated files in review and made `git status`
# unusable. It is all reproducible from source with `crib index .`, so it is build output, not
# source — the same reasoning that already excluded `.crib/index/`.
#
# `.crib/*` (not `.crib/`) with a negation, because git will NOT descend into an excluded DIRECTORY:
# `.crib/` + `!.crib/memory/` silently keeps memory excluded. Excluding the directory's CONTENTS
# instead leaves `.crib/memory/` re-includable.
#
# `.crib/memory/` is the one part that is NOT build output: it is the committed, team-shared memory
# ledger — the product's central promise, and the path `.gitattributes` declares the `kcrib-memory`
# merge driver for. Ignoring it wholesale would have made team memory impossible to share, which is
# the opposite of what this repo exists to do.
.crib/*
!.crib/memory/

# Codex tool state — machine-local, same reasoning.
.codex/
